# source = { run: one }; copy = { ...source } under a type parameter; copy.run(); copy.run = two; source.run(); list = [three]; other = { ...list }; other[0]()
# The copy of a record is a record with the same layout, and one object stands for both: the copy finds what the source holds, and what is stored into the copy counts as stored into a record
# with that layout, so a call through the source may reach it. The copy of anything else is an ordinary object that holds what its source holds.
